The N-gram KMP control logic in src/engines/algorithms.mjs is adapted from
vllm/v1/spec_decode/ngram_proposer.py at the pinned upstream commit.
Copyright contributors to the vLLM project; Apache License 2.0.
Other algorithm chapters are teaching implementations referencing the symbols
listed in docs/ALGORITHMS.md, not executable GPU kernels.

Foundation lessons are independently authored mathematical teaching examples.
Their vLLM references identify applications or comparisons, not implementations
of every illustrated formula. Diffusion background references Ho et al.,
"Denoising Diffusion Probabilistic Models" (2020), arXiv:2006.11239, and
Austin et al., "Structured Denoising Diffusion Models in Discrete State-Spaces"
(2021), arXiv:2107.03006. No paper figures or model weights are bundled.
